Ladybird now gives an item of a horizontal -webkit-box whose flex basis
and width are auto a flex base size of its fit-content width. Run in
Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5, all
three engines do the same.

Blink resolves such an item’s auto flex basis as fit-content in
FlexLayoutAlgorithm::ConstructAndAppendFlexItems(), for a horizontal
box, or a vertical one whose -webkit-box-align isn’t stretch. Gecko
doesn’t apply the flex basis to an item of a legacy box at all: In
nsFlexContainerFrame::GenerateFlexItemForChild(), IsLegacyWebkitBox()
skips the flex basis override, so the item is measured with its own
shrink-wrapped width. WebKit sizes the items of a -webkit-box in
RenderDeprecatedFlexibleBox.
